WEBVTT

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.660
Grandma!

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.300
No!

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.360
It's useless. It's too late.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.230
Grandma!

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.400
What's too late?

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:16.830
Takuto!

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.300
Grandma!

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.060
Don't worry.
She just fainted.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.430
Izumi, you little...
I'm not going to forgive you this time!

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:06.530
Oh boy, now I'm the bad guy.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:13.100
I was just trying to take
her soul for you Meroko.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.700
Izumi...

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.260
More importantly, you remember
all of it now, right, Takuto?

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.630
Or should I call you
Takuto Kira of Route L?

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:28.430
Y-You!
How did you know that?!

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.200
I'd love to hear you sing
one of these days

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.160
before you become a ghost.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.630
<i>Takuto, do you remember</i>
<i>your past now?</i>

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.560
<i>Route L?</i>
<i>Dad and Dr. Wakaoji's band?</i>

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.200
Takuto!

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.660
Did you really remember?!
Hey!

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:03.700
Takuto!

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.630
That's right.
I am Takuto Kira from Route L.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:13.400
Mitsuki, I was the vocalist of the band
that your father and Keichi were in.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.000
You were, Takuto?

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:16.500
Takuto!

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.360
You know what will happen

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.500
if you remember your days
as a human being, don't you?!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:22.360
Yeah.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.200
In that case, why?
Please, forget! Forget all of that!

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.700
It's all right, Meroko.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:29.960
No, it's not all right!

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.960
I don't want you to become a ghost
under any circumstances, Takuto!

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.530
Takuto is gonna be a ghost?

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.830
It can't be helped, Mero.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:47.860
Takuto wasn't cut out to be
a Death Spirit from the start,

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:48.900
so just forget it.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:53.130
But poor guy,
becoming a Death Spirit

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.100
and then getting assigned to
the daughter of his former bandmate.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.930
That's none of your business.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.800
That might not be true.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:06.200
What if I had arranged
for that to happen?

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.160
What?

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.030
You did, Izumi?

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.160
I'm just saying that
hypothetically.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:16.700
I just saw Mitsuki's name on
a pediatrician's list by chance.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.530
Izumi, do you understand
what you've done?

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.430
Do you really think something
like that is forgivable?

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.630
I'm only saying this
hypothetically.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.560
Besides, it's just another dropout
Death Spirit becoming a ghost.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.930
That happens all the time.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.200
If that happened,

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:37.960
you, who loved me before,
could pair up with me again.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.630
That wouldn't be such
a bad thing for you, would it?

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.600
Who would want to
pair up with you?

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:46.030
No, you couldn't turn down
such a good offer, Mero.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.260
Whatever the circumstances,

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.330
you have never contradicted
any of my proposals.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.460
Don't forget that you
betrayed Takuto too.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:01.200
I taught you, didn't I?
That people's feelings are precarious.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.030
Get out of here.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.730
Get out of here!

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:11.360
Takuto!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.500
Why are you getting
so heated up?

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:15.500
Shut up!

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.330
I don't want to see the face
of a scumbag like you!

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:21.230
What a thing to say.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:26.400
I think a person who can't even do
their job right is more of a scumbag.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.030
Shut up!

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.100
The person who
remembered was you.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.060
You're just getting
what you deserve.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.160
Takuto!

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.800
How petty that he can't
sever his ties with his past.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.660
You're the petty one!

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.160
Does being a Death Spirit
make you so important?!

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:01.130
Does reaping people's lives
make you so important?!

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.400
What is so wrong with
remembering my past?

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.630
It's... It's a testament
to my life!

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.300
Stop! Please stop!

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.830
It's not about
being important.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.760
As a Death Spirit,
we must simply accept it.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.260
It's an eternal punishment.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.360
Takuto!

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.700
I'll bid my farewell to
Takuto the Death Spirit.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:48.000
Next time we meet,
you'll probably be a ghost.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.600
Bye bye, Takuto.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:58.330
Damn it...

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.360
Takuto...

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:05.230
Mitsuki, I won't let you die
like this no matter what!

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.900
Are you really okay with everything
just coming to an end like this?

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.800
Are you really okay
with never singing again?!

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:17.930
But... But... Singing...
For what reason?

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:24.960
I no longer have
any reason to sing.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.960
Do you need a reason to sing?

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:32.460
Don't you sing because
you love to sing?

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.100
You love to sing, right?
That's why you've been singing, right?

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.630
So what happened?
It's not like you started to hate singing.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:42.930
And now you're giving it up?

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.600
Are you going to waste
the remainder of your life?

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:49.430
Yeah.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.860
Mitsuki...

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.600
I love to sing,
but I don't want to anymore.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.860
The reason I sang until now
was to get closer to Eichi.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:03.530
But now Eichi is gone.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:08.000
If Eichi in heaven heard you saying that,
he would be very disappointed.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:12.000
He'd think that it was a waste to
fall in love with such a weak person.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.230
You might be right.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.230
But that's fine with me.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:25.130
I was ill with a throat disease,
and if I hadn't met you, Takuto,

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.760
my life would've gone by
without me ever singing.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.830
But we did meet, right?

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.160
And I gave you the body
that allowed you to sing.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.430
Continue singing
to the very end!

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:42.960
You wouldn't be the real you
if you didn't sing.

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:45.830
You'll definitely regret it
if you let that happen.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:47.600
Like me.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:50.660
You have regrets, Takuto?

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:57.260
Yeah. When I was a human,
I got a tumor in my throat just like you.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:02.130
Takuto! You can't remember, Takuto!
You'll become a ghost!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.130
I don't care.
I don't care what happens to me.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.300
Takuto!

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:11.030
If me remembering will make you
want to sing again, Mitsuki,

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:13.430
I will remember
everything for you.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.600
For me?

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.560
I got a tumor in my throat
after Route L disbanded.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:40.130
Even after I went solo,
I continued singing. But...

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:00.600
Eventually my symptoms worsened,
and I was no longer able to sing.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.000
I was devastated.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:11.160
If I had known that
this would happen,

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.560
I wish I had never known
what it was like to sing.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:18.530
I wished I could run away to a world
where there was no music.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:32.430
I went crazy and raced around blindly
trying to run away from everything.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.500
<i>Where is this?</i>

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.060
<i>Jeez! What the heck is this?</i>

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.560
<i>You are Takuto, right?</i>

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.530
<i>Wh-Who the heck are you?</i>

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.230
<i>W-What do you think you're doing?!</i>
<i>Stop that—</i>

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:12.760
<i>Stop...</i>

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>Your memory of the past</i>
<i>has just been sealed off.</i>

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:28.330
<i>Let's go, Death Spirit Takuto...</i>
<i>to a labyrinth of eternal punishment.</i>

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:37.830
I can't believe I died like that!
Why didn't I continue living to the end?!

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.930
I don't want you to have
regrets like I do, Mitsuki.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.160
I don't care if I have regrets.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:52.130
I made up my mind not to sing,
so I will never sing again.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:54.100
Don't you get
what I'm saying yet?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:55.230
You...

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:58.930
Takuto, what's the matter?

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.330
Takuto!

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.800
Don't tell me that his transformation
into a ghost has begun!

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:12.760
Please stop, Takuto! I beg you,
please don't remember anything more!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.000
Meroko!

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.130
Don't worry about me, Meroko.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.330
I must remember.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:27.060
There's more I need
to tell you, Mitsuki.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:28.930
Takuto...

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:50.330
To give Mitsuki
the will to live, eh?

00:12:58.760 --> 00:12:59.760
Mitsuki?!

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:07.260
Takuto!
Don't remember any more!

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:10.500
If you continue like this,
you'll really turn into a ghost!

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:14.460
No! Not until Mitsuki
changes her mind!

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.030
Why?! Why are you
going to that extent?

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.030
Takuto!

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:24.060
Perhaps it's due to the pain, but I'm
starting to remember more and more.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:30.060
You must continue to sing
that song, "Eternal Snow."

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.330
For Aoi and Hazuki.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.960
For my Dad and Mom?

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:35.960
Yeah.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:42.430
When I was a member of Route L,
I, the vocalist was still 12 years old.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.260
The keyboard player
was Keichi Wakaoji.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.400
The guitarist was
your father, Aoi Koga.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:55.360
And Hazuki, your mother
was always with us.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.500
<i>What a beautiful melody.</i>
<i>It sounds like you, Aoi.</i>

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:12.200
<i>I'm so glad you like it.</i>

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:14.300
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:19.460
<i>To Hazuki with love.</i>

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.060
<i>You wrote this song for me?</i>

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.160
<i>Yes.</i>

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:28.860
<i>Takuto!</i>

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:31.930
<i>What is it, Keichi?</i>

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.860
<i>It seems like a waste that</i>
<i>it's just for the music box.</i>

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.700
<i>We should give it some lyrics.</i>

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:48.830
<i>Sure. What kind of image</i>
<i>does it give you, Hazuki?</i>

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.530
<i>Let's see...</i>

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:54.530
<i>Eternal snow...</i>

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.030
<i>Snow that falls forever, huh?</i>

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:01.630
That's how the song, "Eternal Snow,"
came to be written.

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:06.660
Since then, that song became
one of Route L's main songs.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:10.830
That's probably because Aoi and
Hazuki's feelings communicated with us.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:14.000
My dad and my mom's feelings...

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.960
Back then...

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:21.060
I wasn't able to
put it into words,

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.800
but some sort of hot feeling
welled up inside of me.

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:26.160
It was a very strange feeling.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:27.300
You see?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.760
You must continue to
communicate those feelings.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:33.660
Songs aren't concrete things.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:38.960
Unless you sing it,
that song won't exist anywhere.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.760
But...still, it's...

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.330
For goodness sake!

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:48.100
Stop saying things that would
make Aoi and Hazuki sad!

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:49.130
Huh?

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:52.500
The last time I saw Hazuki

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:55.230
was when the two of them
told me they were getting married.

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.030
<i>Really?!</i>

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.830
<i>Congratulations!</i>

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:00.730
<i>Thanks!</i>

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:02.560
<i>Look at this.</i>

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:05.330
<i>I thought we could use</i>
<i>the characters meaning "full moon"</i>

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:06.430
<i>and pronounce it "Mitsuki."</i>

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:07.900
<i>Mitsuki?</i>

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:10.400
<i>The name of our daughter.</i>

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:11.660
<i>Daughter?</i>

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:17.860
<i>I'm not sure it's a girl yet, but I want</i>
<i>to give her the name "Mitsuki."</i>

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:23.500
<i>Even after the moon wanes,</i>
<i>it begins to shine and wax again, right?</i>

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:28.860
<i>I want my child to shine</i>
<i>forever just like the moon.</i>

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:36.400
To shine forever
just like the moon.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.130
Those were their hopes for you
as you were born into this world.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:43.200
Not only Aoi and Hazuki,
but Eichi as well!

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:48.060
And all the people around you today...
We want you to live too!

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:49.500
That's right, Mitsuki!

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.500
Please sing once again!
For everyone's sake!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.830
No. For your own sake!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.000
<i>So you should just be</i>
<i>true to yourself, Mitsuki.</i>

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.930
<i>Because we'll all</i>
<i>make you shine.</i>

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:06.630
<i>I have given</i>
<i>a great deal of thought</i>

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.600
<i>to your request that</i>
<i>I produce Mitsuki's song.</i>

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.530
<i>I will agree on</i>
<i>certain conditions.</i>

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:17.760
<i>We'll do our best together forever!</i>
<i>Okay, Mitsuki?</i>

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:23.460
<i>No!</i>
<i>I-I don't want you to die!</i>

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:26.100
<i>Please, just come back!</i>

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:27.860
<i>Mitsuki!</i>

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.830
For my own sake...

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.600
Be true to myself.

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:55.600
You have to return to how you
were when you were happy.

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:04.700
<i>I have so much desire</i>
<i>to sing right now,</i>

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.360
<i>I feel like my chest is</i>
<i>going to burst open!</i>

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.930
<i>I want to warm people's</i>
<i>hearts with music!</i>

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.100
<i>You're really good at singing,</i>
<i>aren't you, Mitsuki?</i>

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.530
Mitsuki, sing!

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:32.130
You know, they say live music,
don't they? L-I-V-E, live.

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:37.160
To those who have encountered music,
to live is to sing.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.500
To sing is to live.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:50.760
<i>With that, I have told her everything</i>
<i>I needed to tell her.</i>

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:57.800
No!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:03.230
No! You can't
become a ghost!

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.130
What should I do?!

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.930
What do I need to do so that you
don't become a ghost, Takuto?

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:10.500
Stop, Meroko.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:14.530
No! If you're going to become a ghost,
Takuto, I will go with you!

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:15.230
Idiot...

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:17.700
Takuto...

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.430
Mitsuki!

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:22.400
Mrs. Koyama!

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:28.000
Takuto!

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:38.430
How long has it been since
I fell in love with you?

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:47.830
My feelings keep
getting stronger.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:53.800
- Mrs. Koyama! Have you come to?
- I wonder if

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:58.030
- Mitsuki... That song is...
- you can notice them?

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:02.730
- W-Wait a minute. Please let her sing.
- Even though I've

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.800
- Those are Mitsuki's true feelings.
- never mentioned it.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:11.000
- I want to listen to her too.
- They're silent like the snow,

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:13.100
- This is the first time
- but they keep

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:17.000
- I've ever heard her sing.
- building up.

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:23.800
Please forgive me, Hazuki... Aoi...

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.130
I will take care
of your daughter.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:33.460
Hold me tight.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.760
Takuto...
I'm so glad.

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.760
- Yeah.
- If loving someone was

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:46.100
going to feel like this,

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:49.630
I wish I never
found out about love.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:58.330
I love you.
My tears won't stop.

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:03.630
- If this is how it's going to be,
<i>- Everyone is supporting me.</i>

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:08.330
- I wish I had never met you.
<i>- Everyone is making me shine.</i>

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.460
<i>So I'll continue to sing.</i>

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:17.400
<i>Just like the moon that waxes</i>
<i>and shines even after it wanes.</i>

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:11.900
I'm sorry. I don't know what
came over me to ask Izumi.

00:23:12.400 --> 00:23:14.900
It's fine.
You don't have to say anything.

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:17.560
Takuto, thank you!

00:23:18.060 --> 00:23:20.430
Hey, it's no time to be down.

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:24.060
We have the important
task of protecting her!

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:25.360
Yeah!

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:30.030
Next time on Full Moon:
"The Hope to Live."

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:31.500
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
